WEBVTT

0
00:00.260 --> 00:01.330
<v Krista>In this video we're talking</v>

1
00:01.330 --> 00:03.320
about adding and subtracting fractions.

2
00:03.320 --> 00:05.290
The key to adding and subtracting fractions

3
00:05.290 --> 00:07.570
is going to be finding a common denominator.

4
00:07.570 --> 00:10.020
And what we mean by that is equal denominators.

5
00:10.020 --> 00:13.550
So in this first example, we have 1/3 plus 1/2.

6
00:13.550 --> 00:16.080
So the denominator of this fraction is three.

7
00:16.080 --> 00:18.240
The denominator of this fraction is two.

8
00:18.240 --> 00:20.550
But we need the denominators to be the same

9
00:20.550 --> 00:22.530
in order to add the fractions together.

10
00:22.530 --> 00:25.470
Until the denominators are the same, we can't do that.

11
00:25.470 --> 00:28.160
So how do we go about finding a common denominator?

12
00:28.160 --> 00:30.420
Or how do we go about finding a denominator

13
00:30.420 --> 00:31.710
that's going to be equal?

14
00:31.710 --> 00:34.840
What we do is we look for the lowest common multiple

15
00:34.840 --> 00:36.080
of the two denominators.

16
00:36.080 --> 00:39.230
So, again, our denominators are three and two.

17
00:39.230 --> 00:42.660
We need to find the lowest common multiple of three and two.

18
00:42.660 --> 00:44.610
When you have small numbers like this,

19
00:44.610 --> 00:46.990
finding the lowest common multiple is easiest

20
00:46.990 --> 00:49.450
to do by looking at the larger of the two numbers.

21
00:49.450 --> 00:51.080
So our numbers are three and two.

22
00:51.080 --> 00:53.300
Three is larger than two so we're going to look at three.

23
00:53.300 --> 00:55.300
We're going to look at the multiples of three.

24
00:55.300 --> 00:57.680
We're looking for the smallest multiple of three

25
00:57.680 --> 00:59.560
that two's going to go into evenly.

26
00:59.560 --> 01:02.300
So, for example, our multiples of three are three times one,

27
01:02.300 --> 01:03.740
three times two, three times three,

28
01:03.740 --> 01:05.100
three times four, etcetera.

29
01:05.100 --> 01:08.220
So if I take three times one, I'm going to get three.

30
01:08.220 --> 01:10.500
But two doesn't go evenly into three

31
01:10.500 --> 01:12.190
so that one's not going to work.

32
01:12.190 --> 01:13.250
What about three times two?

33
01:13.250 --> 01:15.780
Well, if I do three times two, I get six.

34
01:15.780 --> 01:18.870
Two goes into six evenly, goes in three times.

35
01:18.870 --> 01:22.040
So six is going to be my least common multiple.

36
01:22.040 --> 01:24.020
So with six in mind, I need to figure out

37
01:24.020 --> 01:25.480
what I have to multiply by both

38
01:25.480 --> 01:27.620
of my denominators to get six.

39
01:27.620 --> 01:31.070
In order to get six, I have to multiply three by two

40
01:31.070 --> 01:32.920
because three times two is six.

41
01:32.920 --> 01:36.920
So I'm going to multiply this fraction by two over two.

42
01:36.920 --> 01:38.900
If I do three times two, I'm going to get six,

43
01:38.900 --> 01:40.830
and my denominator, which is what I want.

44
01:40.830 --> 01:43.890
But I can't just multiply the denominator by two.

45
01:43.890 --> 01:46.330
I'm also going to have to multiply the numerator by two.

46
01:46.330 --> 01:48.680
So once I figure out what this number is going to be,

47
01:48.680 --> 01:51.540
I haveta multiply the numerator and the denominator

48
01:51.540 --> 01:52.640
by that number.

49
01:52.640 --> 01:54.210
Now, in order to get six over here,

50
01:54.210 --> 01:56.850
I have to multiply two by three, right?

51
01:56.850 --> 01:59.180
Two times three will give me six.

52
01:59.180 --> 02:00.890
But, again, I can't just do the denominator;

53
02:00.890 --> 02:02.500
I also have to do the numerator.

54
02:02.500 --> 02:04.840
Now I'm going to do my multiplication straight across.

55
02:04.840 --> 02:06.940
I'm going to say two times one.

56
02:06.940 --> 02:08.790
I'm going to say two times three.

57
02:08.790 --> 02:10.960
Over here I'm going to say one times three

58
02:10.960 --> 02:11.980
and two times three.

59
02:11.980 --> 02:13.570
That's how we multiply fractions.

60
02:13.570 --> 02:17.030
So two times one is going to give me two.

61
02:17.030 --> 02:19.370
Two times three is going to give me six.

62
02:19.370 --> 02:22.620
So this fraction here becomes two over six.

63
02:22.620 --> 02:26.400
Then I'm adding to that, one times three gives me three.

64
02:26.400 --> 02:29.790
In the denominator, two times three gives me six.

65
02:29.790 --> 02:32.260
Now notice that I have two different fractions,

66
02:32.260 --> 02:34.810
but the denominators are both six, which is what we wanted.

67
02:34.810 --> 02:36.520
We wanted a common denominator

68
02:36.520 --> 02:38.210
or denominators that were equal.

69
02:38.210 --> 02:40.290
Once we have equal denominators,

70
02:40.290 --> 02:42.460
then we can go ahead and do the addition.

71
02:42.460 --> 02:45.130
So when we do the addition, we add our numerators together.

72
02:45.130 --> 02:48.070
Two plus three is going to be five,

73
02:48.070 --> 02:49.740
and we keep the same denominator.

74
02:49.740 --> 02:51.370
We don't add the denominators.

75
02:51.370 --> 02:53.300
We don't say six plus six is 12.

76
02:53.300 --> 02:55.010
We just keep the same denominators.

77
02:55.010 --> 02:57.690
So this becomes five over six.

78
02:57.690 --> 02:59.280
Let's do another example here.

79
02:59.280 --> 03:02.500
I have eight over 10 minus one over five.

80
03:02.500 --> 03:05.050
I wanta find a common denominator or denominators

81
03:05.050 --> 03:06.530
that are going to be equal to each other.

82
03:06.530 --> 03:07.840
These are pretty small numbers

83
03:07.840 --> 03:10.290
so I'm going to use my lowest common multiple technique

84
03:10.290 --> 03:11.930
that I used in the first example.

85
03:11.930 --> 03:13.640
When I use that technique, I wanta look

86
03:13.640 --> 03:14.930
for the larger of these two numbers.

87
03:14.930 --> 03:17.260
So 10 and five, I have 10 and five.

88
03:17.260 --> 03:19.580
Ten is larger so I'm going to focus on 10.

89
03:19.580 --> 03:21.200
I wanta look at the multiples of 10,

90
03:21.200 --> 03:23.020
and I'm going to start with 10 times one.

91
03:23.020 --> 03:25.360
So if I say 10 times one, I get 10.

92
03:25.360 --> 03:27.720
Obviously, 10 goes into that evenly; it always will.

93
03:27.720 --> 03:29.430
Five also goes into that evenly.

94
03:29.430 --> 03:31.580
Five goes into 10 two times.

95
03:31.580 --> 03:35.140
So I just haveta multiply this fraction here

96
03:35.140 --> 03:36.050
by two over two.

97
03:36.050 --> 03:38.170
If I do five times two, I'm going to get 10.

98
03:38.170 --> 03:40.060
But I also have to multiply the numerator.

99
03:40.060 --> 03:42.660
So I multiply this fraction by two over two.

100
03:42.660 --> 03:45.790
I don't have to multiply this fraction by anything

101
03:45.790 --> 03:48.060
because the denominator is already 10

102
03:48.060 --> 03:50.230
and my common denominator is going to be 10.

103
03:50.230 --> 03:52.560
So now I'm just going to get eight over 10,

104
03:52.560 --> 03:54.150
that's going to stay the same,

105
03:54.150 --> 03:57.640
minus one times two gives me two.

106
03:57.640 --> 04:00.330
Five times two gives me 10.

107
04:00.330 --> 04:02.340
Now I can do my subtraction.

108
04:02.340 --> 04:03.410
I subtract my numerator.

109
04:03.410 --> 04:06.070
So eight minus two gives me six.

110
04:06.070 --> 04:08.620
I keep the common denominator that I already found,

111
04:08.620 --> 04:10.720
and I get 10 in the denominator.

112
04:10.720 --> 04:13.560
So now you could say my final answer is six over 10.

113
04:13.560 --> 04:16.190
However, this fraction isn't in lowest terms.

114
04:16.190 --> 04:17.710
We always need to make sure

115
04:17.710 --> 04:19.320
that our final answer is in lowest terms,

116
04:19.320 --> 04:22.294
and what that means is that both the numerator

117
04:22.294 --> 04:24.240
and the denominator don't have a common factor

118
04:24.240 --> 04:25.510
other than one.

119
04:25.510 --> 04:27.990
In this case, I can divide both the numerator

120
04:27.990 --> 04:29.800
and the denominator by two.

121
04:29.800 --> 04:31.940
If I divide the numerator by two,

122
04:31.940 --> 04:34.570
and I divide the denominator by two,

123
04:34.570 --> 04:36.700
in other words, they have a common factor of two,

124
04:36.700 --> 04:39.020
I get six divided by two is three,

125
04:39.020 --> 04:41.550
and 10 divided by two is five.

126
04:41.550 --> 04:43.230
Now my fraction is in lowest terms

127
04:43.230 --> 04:47.050
because five and three don't have any common factors

128
04:47.050 --> 04:48.090
other than one.

129
04:48.090 --> 04:49.990
And, of course, that makes sense because both

130
04:49.990 --> 04:51.780
of them are prime numbers.

131
04:51.780 --> 04:53.250
Let's look at our last example here.

132
04:53.250 --> 04:55.130
We're going to do this one slightly differently.

133
04:55.130 --> 04:57.500
The reason is because, in the first two examples,

134
04:57.500 --> 04:59.850
we had fairly small numbers for our denominators.

135
04:59.850 --> 05:01.100
We had three and two.

136
05:01.100 --> 05:02.220
We had 10 and five.

137
05:02.220 --> 05:04.270
Those are small enough numbers that we can just look

138
05:04.270 --> 05:06.340
at the larger one, look at its multiples,

139
05:06.340 --> 05:07.760
and find the smallest multiple

140
05:07.760 --> 05:10.280
that the other denominator will go into evenly.

141
05:10.280 --> 05:13.190
But here we have 40 and 65, and finding the multiples

142
05:13.190 --> 05:15.760
of 65 could be a little bit difficult.

143
05:15.760 --> 05:18.850
So instead, we're going to use a prime factorization method.

144
05:18.850 --> 05:20.840
We're going to look at 40 and 65,

145
05:20.840 --> 05:22.570
and factor them into their primes.

146
05:22.570 --> 05:26.950
So if I say 40, I know 40 is 10 times four.

147
05:26.950 --> 05:29.370
I know 10 is five times two.

148
05:29.370 --> 05:32.340
And I know four is two times two.

149
05:32.340 --> 05:34.610
These are all prime numbers so I know I'm done.

150
05:34.610 --> 05:36.330
Let's look at 65.

151
05:36.330 --> 05:40.090
We know 65 is five times 13.

152
05:40.090 --> 05:42.070
Five and 13 are both prime numbers

153
05:42.070 --> 05:43.310
so we know that we're done.

154
05:43.310 --> 05:46.580
Now what we wanta do is build the lowest common multiple

155
05:46.580 --> 05:47.750
from these factors.

156
05:47.750 --> 05:48.810
And here's how we do that.

157
05:48.810 --> 05:50.680
We have to look at the different numbers we have.

158
05:50.680 --> 05:52.360
So we have factors of two.

159
05:52.360 --> 05:54.810
We have factors of five, and we have factors of 13.

160
05:54.810 --> 05:57.340
There's only three different numbers: two, five, and 13.

161
05:57.340 --> 06:00.170
Then we need to look at how many of each factor we have.

162
06:00.170 --> 06:02.470
So if we start with two, we say we have three factors

163
06:02.470 --> 06:03.908
of two over here, we have no factors of two over here.

164
06:03.908 --> 06:07.560
You have to take the larger number of factors

165
06:07.560 --> 06:10.690
so we have to take all three of the factors of two

166
06:10.690 --> 06:14.840
so we're going to take two times two times two.

167
06:14.840 --> 06:18.020
If we had had over here two factors of two

168
06:18.020 --> 06:21.030
with 65, we would've had two factors over here

169
06:21.030 --> 06:23.960
and three over here because three is larger than two.

170
06:23.960 --> 06:25.940
We would've had to take all three of them.

171
06:25.940 --> 06:27.690
We couldn't just take two.

172
06:27.690 --> 06:29.190
So then we look at our factors of five.

173
06:29.190 --> 06:30.840
We have one factor of five over here

174
06:30.840 --> 06:32.670
and one factor of five over here.

175
06:32.670 --> 06:34.654
Those are equal so we just

176
06:34.654 --> 06:35.810
haveta take the one factor of five.

177
06:35.810 --> 06:37.470
Over here we have a factor of 13.

178
06:37.470 --> 06:38.757
We don't have one over here,

179
06:38.757 --> 06:41.800
but because we've got one, we haveta take one.

180
06:41.800 --> 06:44.050
Now we multiply all these values together.

181
06:44.050 --> 06:47.420
That'll give us the least common multiple of 40 and 65,

182
06:47.420 --> 06:49.170
which will be our common denominator.

183
06:49.170 --> 06:52.640
So two times two is four, four times two is eight,

184
06:52.640 --> 06:56.987
eight times five is 40, and 40 times 13 will give us 520.

185
06:58.600 --> 07:01.830
So 520 will be our common denominator.

186
07:01.830 --> 07:06.750
Now if we take 520 and we divide it by 40, we get 13.

187
07:06.750 --> 07:09.810
That means that we have to multiply this first fraction

188
07:09.810 --> 07:14.600
by 13 over 13 in order to get 520 in the denominator.

189
07:14.600 --> 07:16.790
Thirteen times 40 is 520.

190
07:16.790 --> 07:21.270
If we take 520, and we divide it by 65, we get eight.

191
07:21.270 --> 07:24.690
So if we multiply this fraction by eight over eight,

192
07:24.690 --> 07:28.230
then we'll get 65 times eight or 520 in the denominator.

193
07:28.230 --> 07:31.900
And now we'll have a common denominator of 520.

194
07:31.900 --> 07:33.370
Now we just do our multiplication.

195
07:33.370 --> 07:36.847
So we say 13 times 17 will give us 221.

196
07:38.000 --> 07:42.780
We know 13 times 40 is 520, our common denominator.

197
07:42.780 --> 07:46.880
Then we say 23 times eight, which will give us 160 and 24

198
07:46.880 --> 07:51.650
or 184, and we know our common denominator is going to be 520,

199
07:51.650 --> 07:54.850
65 times eight gives us 520.

200
07:54.850 --> 07:57.160
So you can see now with this common denominator

201
07:57.160 --> 07:58.960
we just add the numerators together.

202
07:58.960 --> 08:02.291
So 221 plus 184 is 405,

203
08:02.291 --> 08:04.610
so we get 405;

204
08:04.610 --> 08:08.020
and then our common denominator of 520.

205
08:08.020 --> 08:09.630
Now we just need to make sure our fraction

206
08:09.630 --> 08:10.630
is in lowest terms.

207
08:10.630 --> 08:13.560
We can see right away that both 405 and 520

208
08:13.560 --> 08:15.680
are going to be divisible by five.

209
08:15.680 --> 08:20.680
So if we divide 405 by five, we're going to get 81.

210
08:20.950 --> 08:24.077
If we divide 520 by five, we're going to get 104.

211
08:24.970 --> 08:28.760
Since 81 and 104 don't have any common factor

212
08:28.760 --> 08:31.710
other than one, we know our fraction is in lowest terms,

213
08:31.710 --> 08:33.463
and that'll be our final answer.